(BAS-56 - get the period count wrong and nothing tells you: both halves
 below compile cleanly and run to exit 0. Too few periods and the
 following statement is absorbed into a clause you thought you had left
 (nothing prints); too many and it escapes one you meant to stay in (it
 prints when it should not have). No error, no warning, either way.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS-56.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   escaped a clause it was meant to stay in
)
(too few: absorbed into a false If, so it never prints)
a number called n is 0.
If n is equal to 1 then,
    If n is equal to 1 then, print "innermost".
print "absorbed, never printed".

(too many: the second period escapes the outer If, so it prints even
 though the condition that guarded it is true and the statement was meant
 to stay inside)
a number called m is 1.
If m is equal to 1 then,
    If m is equal to 2 then, print "inner"..
print "escaped a clause it was meant to stay in".
